WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Follow the current Tally interface. Simple and Advanced use the
same saved settings. Pause at any step.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:16.699
Use Minecraft Java Edition 1.21.11, Fabric Loader, the matching
Fabric API mod, and Java 21. The written

00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:25.000
guide links the official Fabric instructions. Use the Fabric
setup for your own launcher.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.779
Open the Tally releases page on GitHub
(github.com/GoatTech-42/tally/releases). Download

00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:33.202
tally-1.21.11-beta-candidate.jar from the v1.0.0-beta release
for Minecraft 1.21.11 and save it without

00:00:33.202 --> 00:00:37.669
extracting. SHA256SUMS is published beside it. This is a beta,
not a final release. Normal keyless setup

00:00:37.669 --> 00:00:39.000
does not need a manual API key.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:47.695
Close Minecraft. Open the game folder for the installation you
actually launch. Put the Tally beta jar and

00:00:47.695 --> 00:00:56.309
the matching Fabric API jar in its mods folder. Create mods if
missing. Keep only one Tally jar. Updating

00:00:56.309 --> 00:01:00.000
does not require deleting your configuration.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:08.965
Launch your Fabric installation and join DonutSMP. Enable the
sidebar scoreboard in the server settings so

00:01:08.965 --> 00:01:17.000
Tally can read your balance. Press B. Check Minecraft Controls
if you changed that key binding.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:28.805
New installs open Start here. To return later, press B, choose
Settings, then Help & setup. Choose Set up

00:01:28.805 --> 00:01:36.000
trading. Do not search for a separate START HERE navigation tab.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:45.736
Enter maximum per trade and maximum session spend. Choose your
own amounts; these screenshot values are

00:01:45.736 --> 00:01:55.000
examples, not recommendations. Review & continue opens the
second step. It does not start trading.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:02.756
Review protections opens Evasion. Read its options and review
Staff Watch separately if you use it. Return

00:02:02.756 --> 00:02:10.585
to setup afterward. Discord is an optional connection; the
hosted Swarm service is retired. Opening a guide

00:02:10.585 --> 00:02:13.000
does not start or resume trading.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:23.176
On Review & Start, check your limits and readiness. This offline
demonstration has not joined a server, so

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:33.352
Start is disabled. On your client, read the actual blocker.
Choose Start trading only when ready. Existing

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:37.000
recovery and trade checks still apply.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:47.800
Open Trading, then Trade for status and controls. A connected
client is not necessarily trading. Read the

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:55.000
actual reason before taking action. End is the default emergency
stop.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:08.925
Open Settings, Help & setup, then Show menus + hotbar. Only
those two display options change. This is not a

00:03:08.925 --> 00:03:14.000
full settings or trading-history reset.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:24.948
Simple groups order management, trading style, action pace and
order batch ceiling. Custom means existing

00:03:24.948 --> 00:03:36.000
values stay as they are. Choosing an option opens an exact
change preview. Only Apply saves those changes.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:45.808
Advanced keeps every individual setting. Choose a category or
search. Warnings explain interactions such as

00:03:45.808 --> 00:03:55.067
disabled bidding or sizing limits. A batch ceiling is a maximum,
not a promised order size or profit.

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:58.000
Switching views changes nothing.
